From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 02:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ipc/namespace: assign user_ns BEFORE mq_init_ns

This CAF 4.4 tree backported the 4.9-style user_ns-aware mqueue_mount /
mount_ns() (6-arg form taking ns->user_ns), but kept the 4.4 create_ipc_ns
ordering where mq_init_ns() runs BEFORE ns->user_ns is assigned.

mq_init_ns() kern-mounts mqueue for the new ipc namespace; the superblock
records s_user_ns = ns->user_ns. With the old ordering that field is
uninitialized kmalloc garbage. Every later userspace mount of mqueue inside
the new ipc namespace then matches that superblock in sget_userns() but fails
the user_ns equality check -> -EBUSY.

Effect on device (2026-09-19, kretprobe-verified): any container runtime
that creates CLONE_NEWIPC and mounts mqueue (docker/runc default OCI spec)
fails with

  error mounting "mqueue" to rootfs at "/dev/mqueue": ... device or resource
  busy

Fix by moving the user_ns assignment above mq_init_ns(), matching vanilla
4.9+ create_ipc_ns(). On the mq_init_ns failure path, drop the reference.

Verified on NX563J Ubuntu 24.04 chroot: after this patch `docker run` with
the default (private ipc namespace) spec completes.
---
 ipc/namespace.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ipc/namespace.c b/ipc/namespace.c
--- a/ipc/namespace.c
+++ b/ipc/namespace.c
@@ -34,8 +34,10 @@ static struct ipc_namespace *create_ipc_ns(struct user_namespace *user_ns,
 	ns->ns.ops = &ipcns_operations;

 	atomic_set(&ns->count, 1);
+	ns->user_ns = get_user_ns(user_ns);
 	err = mq_init_ns(ns);
 	if (err) {
+		put_user_ns(ns->user_ns);
 		ns_free_inum(&ns->ns);
 		kfree(ns);
 		return ERR_PTR(err);
@@ -46,7 +48,5 @@ static struct ipc_namespace *create_ipc_ns(struct user_namespace *user_ns,
 	msg_init_ns(ns);
 	shm_init_ns(ns);

-	ns->user_ns = get_user_ns(user_ns);
-
 	return ns;
 }
